    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100-a9">

                <pb facs="0216" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg112"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The diplomatic corps to Mizner</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9 in No.
                    170.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-31"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 31,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: In view of the incidents connected
                    with the death of General Barrundia on board of the Pacific Mail steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Acapulco</hi>, we hand to Your Excellency this
                    expression of our sympathy and friendship.</p>
                <p>Witnesses of the lofty aims that have animated Your Excellency in so grave and
                    delicate an affair, and understanding your procedure in trying to secure the
                    life of the above-named general, inasmuch as it was impossible to prevent his
                    arrest, which had been ordered, we consider it our duty to extend to you this
                    assurance.</p>
                <p>We take advantage of the opportunity thus offered to assure you of our high
                    consideration and esteem.</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">José Ma. Castro</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Minister of Costa Rica</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Larios</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Minister of Nicaragua</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julio de Arellano</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Minister of Spain</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. Reynaud</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Chargé d’ Affaires of Prance.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ate. Halewyck</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Chargé d’ Affaires of Belgium</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur Chapman</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Chargé d’ Affaires of Great
                                Britain</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul Schmaeck</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires of Germany.</hi></item>
                            <item>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing B. Mizner</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">United States Minister.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
